#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/delivery/next-iterations.md:75
msgid ""
"维护责任由 Codex 全部承担，`.github/maintainer-roles.json` 使用 `agent_managed` "
"策略。十人角色保留为领域与容量划分，不再要求实名账号；安全、 制造和现场接口也由同一维护责任覆盖，产品权限／流程留在外部应用仓库。"
msgstr ""
"Codex assumes all maintenance responsibility; `.github/maintainer-"
"roles.json` uses `agent_managed`. Ten-person roles remain domain/capacity "
"divisions without requiring named accounts. The same maintenance "
"responsibility covers security, manufacturing and field interfaces; product "
"permissions/processes remain in external application repositories."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/delivery/next-iterations.md:79
msgid ""
"`python tools/maintenance/ownership.py --require-assigned` 验证负责 agent、 "
"路径覆盖、备用领域和强制门禁。GoogleTest／GoogleMock、配置、ARM、预算、SDK 和证据身份检查继续执行。该策略不生成虚构 "
"CODEOWNERS，不声明独立人工评审； GitHub branch rules 与 required checks 的实际配置状态仍须远程核实。 "
"具体命令见[维护工具](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/tools/maintenance/README.md)。"
msgstr ""
"`python tools/maintenance/ownership.py --require-assigned` verifies "
"responsible agents, path coverage, backup domains and required gates. "
"GoogleTest/GoogleMock, configuration, ARM, budget, SDK and evidence-identity"
" checks continue. This policy fabricates no CODEOWNERS and claims no "
"independent human review. Actual GitHub branch-rule/required-check "
"configuration still needs remote verification. Commands are in [maintenance "
"tools](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/tools/maintenance/README.md)."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/delivery/next-iterations.md:85
msgid ""
"Issue 描述具体触发和可观察结果；PR 明确源／配置／依赖／工具与影响的合同。每次 commit 自动检查 staged 内容和 "
"Conventional Commit，CI 用同一整文件规范。 新行为和缺陷修复必须 TDD，主机合同采用 "
"GoogleTest／GoogleMock；Python 工具 保留 unittest。新增用例先实际 RED，再最小修复 "
"GREEN；机械门禁不证明历史编辑 顺序，PR 记录命令、失败原因和原始日志。中断、生命周期、持久化和并发变更要有 真实 failure-path "
"回归。nightly/正式候选的测量、离线构建和 station 结果独立封存， 生产发布不由普通平台 CI 自动提升。"
msgstr ""
"Issues describe concrete triggers and observable results. PRs state "
"source/config/dependency/tool identities and affected contracts. Each commit"
" automatically checks staged content and Conventional Commit; CI uses the "
"same whole-file standard. New behavior and bug fixes require TDD: "
"GoogleTest/GoogleMock for host contracts, unittest for Python tools. New "
"cases run RED first, then a minimal GREEN fix. Mechanical gates do not prove"
" historical editing order; PRs record commands, failure reasons and raw "
"logs. IRQ, lifecycle, persistence and concurrency changes need actual "
"failure-path regressions. Nightly/formal-candidate measurements, offline "
"builds and station results are sealed separately; ordinary platform CI does "
"not automatically promote production releases."
